<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose slightly in the one to twelve-month maturities, while the one to two weeks were unchanged, traders said.</p>
<p>A trader said the changes were brought about by the softening of borrowing rates on the dollar. This led to a wider interest rate differential between the peso and the dollar from which swap points are computed.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 MARCH 5		 MARCH 4</p>
<p>    1 W		9  5/8		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9  5/8		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		9 11/16		 9  5/8</p>
<p>    2 M		9  3/4		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9 13/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10 1/16		 10</p>
<p>    12M		10  5/16		10  1/4</p>
<p>    VAL		6-Mar		   5-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
